WEBVTT

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.940
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.940
<i>The Nautilus anchors off an island to
replenish dwindling supplies.</i>

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:36.110
<i>By chance, an enemy Garfish is
also anchored off this island.</i>

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.450
<i>Marie and Sanson are found by Neo
Atlanteans, and pursued into camp.</i>

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.410
<i>An enemy soldier starts firing his
rifle at Nadia and the others.</i>

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:47.290
<i>In response, Nemo calmly shoots
and kills the enemy soldier.</i>

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.760
Unidentified ship ahead at 2 o'clock!

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.390
We caught them at last.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.310
Yes, it's probably the Garfish.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:08.020
Right, there's no other ship that
can operate at this depth.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.480
Other submarines are like
toys in comparison.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.070
Shall we go after them, Captain?

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:18.360
Of course! Change bearing to
2 o'clock! Full speed ahead!

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.820
Aye aye, Sir!

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.280
All hands to Code 2 battle positions!

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.870
All hands to Code 2 battle positions!

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.830
I repeat! All hands to Code 2
battle positions!

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:31.040
All non-combatants proceed
to Block 3 shelters!

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.000
Looks like we're going out on
another killing campaign.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:38.220
You shouldn't talk like that.
We're after the murderous Garfish.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.890
What's the difference?!
I cannot excuse him.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:42.850
Just despicable!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:44.600
But...

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.690
He's a murderer! I don't care
what reasons he gives!

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:55.270
If Captain Nemo hadn't shot that
soldier, he might have killed you.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.650
I'd rather be shot than
see a person killed.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.820
You're being unreasonable
when you say that!

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.910
Marie! MARIE!

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.920
Doctor, how is she?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.630
I heard that Marie collapsed!

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.050
Marie...

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.720
Marie! Doctor! Marie...
Marie's all right, isn't she?

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.640
Well, tell me, Doctor!

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.350
It may be tropical fever.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:28.640
Tropical fever?

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.100
The name isn't important! She's going
to get well quickly, right?

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.860
That's hard to say.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.440
What do you mean?

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.410
Use one of your wonder pills
and make her well again!

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.410
It's a very rare disease.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.160
I'm afraid we don't have an antidote
for it onboard this ship.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.370
You must have!

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.620
Then, what'll happen to Marie?

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:56.630
Hanson, you always talk about your
inventions, the power of science.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.090
Can't you do something?!

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.800
This is out of my field.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.510
No use in an emergency!

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.890
Marie, what's the matter? Does it hurt?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.060
Marie...

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.240
Damn!

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.780
Isn't there someone who can
do something for her?

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.950
Maybe...

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.910
Maybe? Maybe what?

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:32.500
Maybe Captain Nemo can help her.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.040
He is a specialist in tropical
fever and marine biology.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.420
I understand. Captain Nemo can help.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.220
Nadia!

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.140
Nadia!

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:50.350
Captain Nemo! Marie...
Please save Marie!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.140
Marie has collapsed from
tropical fever!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.070
The doctor told us you may
know how to help her.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.980
Please save Marie!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.950
Captain Nemo!

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:10.660
To treat a person with tropical fever,
we must go to Reef 64.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.620
But we're only 6,000 meters from
overtaking the Garfish.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.710
We've finally located the Garfish
after ten days of hunting.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.340
We can't let it get away.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:23.800
For a reason like that?

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.760
For us, this is the most
important objective.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.720
For that, you are willing
to sacrifice Marie?!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.180
Your objective is to destroy the Garfish?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.350
There are human beings
on that ship, right?

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.900
You're going to commit murder again?

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.270
Which is more important, to kill
people or to save them?

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.280
Answer me!

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.240
Nadia, please calm down and listen.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:50.910
Nadia?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.740
Nadia!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:58.000
Nadia, hang in there! Nadia!

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.880
Nadia and Marie have fallen sick?

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:02.960
Senorita?

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.920
Whatever happened?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.930
It's tropical fever.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.310
What kind of a disease is it?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.770
They'll both die within two days.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.230
They can't!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.820
Without medicine, there's
nothing I can do.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:28.820
I understand! I'll go and
see the Captain.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.620
Wait just a minute, Senorita.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.070
I'll go!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.660
Why you?

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.540
There's something I feel isn't right.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:42.130
Look at this poor kid suffering
from an awful disease,

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.130
and no one, not even the captain,
has come to see her.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:51.840
Can't they even say one
gentle word to her?!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:58.140
Are the people on this ship a
bunch of heartless souls?!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.940
What? Nadia too?

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.690
Yes, she caught it from Marie.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.950
I see. If so, both of them have
only two more days.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.490
We're within 3,000 meters
of the Garfish.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.120
We'll be within firing range
in two minutes.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.250
Which is more important, to kill
people or to save them?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:20.670
There are no obstacles in the way.
All engines at full speed.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.830
All hands are in full battle positions.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.340
Change heading 180 degrees, and
proceed to Reef 64 at full speed.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.010
What's that?!

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.140
Are you going to let the
Garfish get away?!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:44.610
You've sacrificed much to overthrow
Neo Atlantis and to kill Gargoyle.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.480
Are you going to give it all up
on account of a child?!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:55.450
Thirteen years ago I vowed vengeance
for my parents and my little brother.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.450
Did you hear my orders?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.460
Yes, Sir.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:07.920
Change heading 180 degrees,
and proceed to Reef 64.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.510
Commencing turn.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.470
Bearing fixed at 125. Target, Reef 64.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.680
Distance to Garfish 5,000
meters and increasing.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.940
First Officer...

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:23.600
Sir?

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.400
Take over the command.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.860
Yes, Sir.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.700
Well, we can go after the Garfish
again some other time.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.320
That depends on how well
you do your job.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.990
I guess you're right.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.910
Right, Helmsman?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.870
Just kidding!

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.340
Reef 64?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.550
Then Nadia and Marie will be saved?!

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:03.430
Right! We'll reach it within a day
so they should both be okay.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:04.270
That's wonderful!

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:05.900
We won!

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.110
I'm going to see Miss Electra.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.730
Look after King, please.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:15.240
Hey, wait! Don't go now. Wait!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.910
Why don't I think things through?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.880
I agree with you. I think Captain
Nemo has changed too.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:33.880
I was surprised when he ordered an
about face with the Garfish there.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.800
But I don't think his order
was a mistake.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:43.890
If we let those poor kids die so we
could pursue our objective,

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:47.270
we'd be acting just like Gargoyle.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:53.150
I'd like to get revenge for my son
and grandchild too,

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.900
but that doesn't mean I can
do anything I want.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.330
You know, Electra, I trust Captain Nemo.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:05.790
The only reason we're alive today is
because he was there to save us.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:13.500
I wonder what kind of a man
Captain Nemo is?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.510
It's clear to see.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.970
An unlikeable guy.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.430
Is he really?

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:23.140
He's a middle-aged man making
eyes at our Senorita.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.560
Isn't it the other way around?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.020
Shut up!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:33.360
Anyway, when you grow up, Jean,
don't ever become a guy like him.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:37.440
Try to become a gentleman like me.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.320
I wouldn't recommend that.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.910
Keep quiet!

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:45.910
In other words, he isn't
much of a man.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.870
But he killed a man.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:52.840
Naturally, there's a war going on.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:57.090
In war, they keep killing each other
until one side gives up.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:03.890
The crew on board this ship are all
prepared to kill and be killed.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.560
A war where people die...

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.270
Jean...

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.900
Is it such a rare thing,
to see people die?

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:20.200
In my home, there were people dying
everyday, from illness and war.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.570
Including my parents.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:29.000
It's not a rare thing to see people die,
especially in this age.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.800
Point SP 22. RP 40.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.010
We have reached Reef 64!

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:50.520
Stop both engines at the cave.
Prepare the diving sphere.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.310
Aye aye!

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.950
Captain Nemo, we'd like to go as well!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.670
It's going to be very dangerous.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.250
We understand.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:16.880
I guess it's no use arguing.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.840
Put on that diving gear. As soon
as you're ready, we'll go.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.420
Yes, Sir!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:28.680
Pressure valve, okay.
Air supply tube, normal.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.220
All instruments in order.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.690
The diving sphere will be stationed
at the entrance of the cave.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.810
You'll send messages between the
collecting party and the Nautilus.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:37.770
Understand?

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:38.440
Aye aye.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:43.570
Captain, preparations are complete.
We can start anytime.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.910
Good! Are you fellows ready?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:46.950
Yes, Sir!

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:50.330
What are you two doing?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.290
Tada!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.040
King wanted to go too.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.130
When did you prepare his gear?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.420
We've been thinking about this ever
since we saw the diving gear.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.090
We didn't just think about it, we
made it, which makes us...

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.930
Geniuses!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.510
Will you two stop kidding?
Marie and Nadia are dying!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.810
Sorry.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:14.350
Gentlemen, we don't have much time.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.100
There are a few things to tell you
about underwater conversation.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.320
If the distance is under five meters,

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:24.820
you can communicate through the
speaker on top of your helmets.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:28.030
We should have put a speaker
on King's helmet too.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.780
What a marvelous invention!

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:34.830
Over five meters, the voice is distorted
and you can't understand.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.540
In that case, you use this light.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.210
Are you all versed in Morse Code?

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.010
Yes, Sir!

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:43.670
Yes.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:47.130
Good. Just one more thing.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:53.350
Reef 64 is basically safe,
but not absolutely so.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:58.190
Each must look after himself. In the
water, none can come and save you.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.020
Yes, Sir!

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:02.360
All right, everyone into the
pressure chamber.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.190
Yes, Sir!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.360
Yes, this is the bridge.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.410
It's me.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.740
The party is in the pressure chamber.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.200
All preparations are go.
Open the valves.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.660
Aye, Sir. We'll start the water flow.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.540
There's water coming in.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:27.930
Don't panic, King.
Try to breathe slowly.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.230
Water inflow complete.
The chamber is full.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.190
All right, let's go.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:56.790
Golly, it's so deep! I wonder
how wide it is?

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.960
Jean, hurry! We haven't much time.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:01.630
Yes, Sir! I'm sorry.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.090
Let's get a move on.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.090
Sorry.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.930
The sphere has been disconnected.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.150
Distance to sea bottom,
about thirty meters.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.570
Gosh, I've never seen
such fish before.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:33.870
They're all thought to have gone
extinct many eons ago.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.540
Probably due to sea currents
and contours,

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:41.250
Reef 64 hasn't been in contact with the
outside ocean for millions of years.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:45.500
This is truly a lost world. I read about
such a place when I was a kid.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:49.670
To a paleontologist, it's
a dream come true.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.930
What's this?

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.260
It's called the snow of the deep sea.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.310
It's made up mostly of dead
micro-organisms.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:00.310
I find it hard to believe.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.100
They emit light after death.

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.980
Truly a mystery of life and death.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:08.690
Nadia would have loved
to see this too.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:21.870
Hurry.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:22.620
Yes, Sir!

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:30.010
This is Diving Sphere One.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:33.090
The search party has entered
the side opening.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.680
Roger. Please remain at your station.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.470
Roger.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.810
This is amazing, a forest of seaweed.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.770
Sanson, why'd you bring that gun?

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:50.480
Oh, I borrowed it just in case
we run into something.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.450
You certainly like to carry weapons.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.660
Their oxygen supply will
last another hour.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.830
I hope nothing happens.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:11.510
Wow, impressive! It certainly
looks deep.

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:14.170
Probably more than a thousand meters.

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.840
Do we have to go in there?

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:21.060
No, our target is that little
opening down there.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.980
Whew! Thank goodness!

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.560
But how do we get over there?

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:26.940
Like this.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.490
Amazing!

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.740
But how do we get back?

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.820
See these pins on the shoulder
of your diving gear.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:42.080
If you pull them out, an air
balloon will come out.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:45.040
Really? So that's what those are for.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.960
We should have had them for King too.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:49.380
I'll go first.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.250
How cool!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.800
Are you okay?

00:17:58.800 --> 00:17:59.680
Yes, Sir.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:03.270
Good, but let's hurry.
We don't have much time.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.740
Is this the medicinal herb?

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.910
Yes, no question about it.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.660
Then, they'll be well again?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:23.540
That's great!

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.500
Lucky!

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.130
This is enough. Our mission is over.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:35.840
Let's head back.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.550
Right!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.850
What is it, King? You want to go first?

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.270
Well, okay.

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:49.560
King!

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.280
That thing's huge!

00:18:58.280 --> 00:18:59.360
It's a dinicthys.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.070
It belongs to the Devonian Era.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:07.000
It's frightening and big,
but it's still only a fish!

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.290
We can't fight it.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.540
How can we tell if we don't try?

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.130
Here we go.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:22.890
It's covered with a body
armor of hard skin.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.310
That gun won't even scratch it.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.980
Captain Nemo, what do we do?
We can't get out.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.810
I've got it! Everyone,
douse your lights.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:36.440
It's attracted to us because,
to it, light means food.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.440
They're awfully late.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:42.450
I wonder if something has happened.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:48.660
Some animals are phototaxic,
instinctively heading for light.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:54.170
I see. As soon as we doused our
lights, it left the cave area.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:58.170
We're going to use this item
and that habit against it.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.260
What is that?

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.970
It's a pressure switch. If l
drop this into the hole,

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:08.520
the pressure will activate the switch,
turning this light on.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:12.270
And it will attract that thing
away from us!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.940
It's too narrow for a grown-up,
but maybe...

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:21.490
Jean!

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:22.400
Yes, Sir.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:27.330
It's dangerous, but only you
and King can do this.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:28.870
Will you try?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.620
Yes, I will.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.830
Thanks.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:40.550
Please hurry back, Captain Nemo!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:45.220
This is bad. We have only five
minutes of oxygen left.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.350
It's all up to you, Jean.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:56.190
It's getting hard to breathe. We must
be running out of oxygen.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.400
It's only a little bit more.
Let's go, King.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:09.120
I'll fix this to the rock with a wire.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:14.750
It's a little lengthy, but I don't have
anything to cut it with.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:17.710
Okay, now!

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.500
Beginning operation!

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:24.630
King!

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:33.980
Jean!

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:39.560
The wire won't break!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:41.440
It's amazingly strong!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:45.320
Our only chance!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.120
We're safe.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:03.960
As soon as we get back, we're
locked up in a place like this.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:08.130
We'll get divers' cramp unless we're
decompressed slowly.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:11.140
This time, we owe our
lives to this boy.

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:13.930
Thanks, Jean and King.

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:18.140
No, we owe our lives to you.
Thank you.

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:21.480
It's not us. You should thank
Captain Nemo.

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:24.480
I couldn't have saved you by myself.

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.610
Captain Nemo?

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:30.570
The fever has dropped.
Both are out of danger now.

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:34.290
Oh, I'm so happy! I was so worried!

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:37.580
Nadia and Marie, we heard you're
both all right now!

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:40.540
Can't you be more quiet?

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:43.590
Don't be like that!

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:45.050
I'm happy to see you
well again, Marie.

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:48.680
Nadia, is it all right for you to be up?

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:51.430
Of course, and thanks.

00:22:52.430 --> 00:22:53.970
Gladly.

00:22:55.180 --> 00:22:59.480
Captain Nemo risked his life getting
the medicinal herbs.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:01.230
You should be grateful.

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:03.320
I don't believe you!

00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:04.480
It's true.

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:09.990
But it was Jean who saved
Captain Nemo.

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:12.030
Please, leave me out.

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:17.910
I see. Captain Nemo...

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:25.050
Captain Nemo, I've returned
our course to SB-60.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:27.130
Speed is set at one-third.

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:30.180
Excuse me.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:31.470
First Officer...

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:34.850
I'm sorry.

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:36.510
What for?

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.060
I have every faith in the
decisions you make.

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:41.520
I see.
